================================================================================
About this work
================================================================================

Polaris is a reference implementation of a national identity token system —
what a sovereign-grade identity layer would look like if you designed it
from first principles in 2026, knowing what we now know about post-quantum
cryptography, zero-knowledge proofs, append-only audit, and the failure
modes of every CBDC pilot.

Built as the portfolio piece for SCS-230 (Database Management Systems) at
Seton Hill University, Spring 2026. The course is the occasion; the
engineering bar is production-grade.

The constitution (the ten hard constraints C1–C10 plus the Vocation)
lives in MISSION.md. The audit-of-record principle —
that every state-changing decision in the system has a schema element or
equivalent artifact reconstructing operation history — lives in
DEVNOTES/audit-of-record.md.

